## Color and Clarity at 3ct Radiant

The [radiant cut engagement rings](/radiant-cut-engagement-rings) guide establishes G-VS2 as the grade floor for this shape. At 3ct, the floor holds, but color requires more care.

**Color at 3ct radiant:** At 9.2mm face-up, the stone has more surface for color to express itself than at any smaller weight in this series. G remains correct in yellow and rose gold. In white gold or platinum, F is more defensible at 3ct than at 2ct or 2.5ct. The difference between G and F is subtle but more perceptible at this size in cold metal.

**Clarity at 3ct radiant:** VS2 is still reliably eye-clean at 3ct in a radiant cut. The 70-facet brilliant pattern continues to hide inclusions. VS1 adds a certainty layer — particularly valuable if you are purchasing without viewing HD video. Do not go below VS2 at 3ct.

**Color by metal at 3ct:**

| Metal | Recommended Color | What this means |
|-------|-----------------|----------------|
| 14K / 18K White Gold | G or F | F provides extra color protection at 3ct in cold metal — more defensible than at 2ct |
| Platinum | F or E | Platinum's blue-white tone amplifies color at 9.2mm face-up — E is the safest choice |
| 14K / 18K Yellow Gold | G or H | Yellow gold masks warmth — G reads white; H acceptable but G is the cleaner pick |
| Rose Gold | G minimum | G is the floor in rose gold at 3ct; warmer tones accumulate at this size — do not go below G |

At 3ct, VS1 is the practical clarity choice if you value certainty. VS2 is defensible in a radiant cut.

